 ],
 "notes": "\"in us-east-1\" is not checked: the plan region attribute is absent from these provider versions' normalised plans. sg_ssh_only enforces \"SSH only from within the VPC CIDR\": every ingress rule must either use only the VPC CIDR (or a security-group source) or not cover port 22 (tcp/udp range excluding 22, or ICMP); an all-protocol rule from outside the VPC fails. Its branches are per encoding (inline list, aws_security_group_rule, aws_vpc_security_group_ingress_rule); a template mixing encodings is judged only on the encoding that passes. sg_egress requires every egress rule to target only the VPC CIDR. \"associated only with the public subnet\" is checked positively only: associations plan with unknown IDs and selectors cannot filter by refs, so an extra association of the public route table cannot be detected; assoc_pub and assoc_rt are also not bound to one association for the same reason."
}